@startuml Visitor

interface Shape {
    +accept(visitor: ShapeVisitor&) : void
}

class Circle {
    -radius_ : double
    +accept(visitor: ShapeVisitor&) : void
}

class Square {
    -side_ : double
    +accept(visitor: ShapeVisitor&) : void
}

interface ShapeVisitor {
    +visit(circle: Circle&) : void
    +visit(square: Square&) : void
}

class AreaVisitor {
    +visit(circle: Circle&) : void
    +visit(square: Square&) : void
}

class DescribeVisitor {
    +visit(circle: Circle&) : void
    +visit(square: Square&) : void
}

Shape <|.. Circle
Shape <|.. Square
ShapeVisitor <|.. AreaVisitor
ShapeVisitor <|.. DescribeVisitor

Circle ..> ShapeVisitor : accept() calls visit(*this)
Square ..> ShapeVisitor : accept() calls visit(*this)

note right of ShapeVisitor
  Double dispatch: accept()
  virtually dispatches on the
  element's concrete type,
  then visit() overload
  resolution picks the right
  operation for that type.
end note

@enduml